          {
            "msg_id": "M34",
            "speaker_id": 87396,
            "reply_to": "M33",
            "text": "Thanks. I've had a quick look. \nA2 looks comprehensive. \nA4 is clear and covers the essentials for handovers. \nFor A7, the monitoring log, could we simplify the rating scale? A 1-5 scale might be too nuanced for a quick handover. Maybe a simple 3-point scale like 'struggling / okay / thriving' would get better compliance from staff on busy shifts.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A2",
              "A4",
              "A7"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "bulb",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M35",
            "speaker_id": 36599,
            "reply_to": "M33",
            "text": "I agree with 87396 on A7. A simple scale is better. For the handover checklist A4, it's good. Can we add one checkbox for 'Medication updates' just to be safe? It's something that can get missed between shifts.",
            "mentions": [
              87396
