        "thread_goal": "Plan and coordinate vocational skills taster modules within the weekly schedule.",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M48",
            "speaker_id": 87396,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Hi team, I've put together the vocational skills taster module pack (A6) for review. This covers T5. I'm proposing three initial modules: \n1. Basic Cooking & Kitchen Safety (ties into the bake-off idea)\n2. CV & Job Application Basics\n3. Simple Woodworking & Tool Safety",
            "mentions": [
              87939,
              36599,
              4543,
              483681
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A6",
              "T5"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "star-struck",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M49",
            "speaker_id": 87396,
            "reply_to": "M48",
            "text": "Looking at the main schedule A5, I suggest we run the Cooking module on Wednesdays at 4pm, and the CV basics on Mondays at 4pm. The woodworking might need a weekend slot if we need more time and focus. What do you think?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A5"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M50",
            "speaker_id": 36599,
            "reply_to": "M48",
            "text": "These look great. The kids will love the woodworking one. Sam in particular is very hands-on. The cooking one is a great life skill.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M51",
            "speaker_id": 87939,
            "reply_to": "M49",
            "text": "The timings for cooking and CV basics work perfectly with the schedule A5. A weekend slot for woodworking is a good idea to avoid rushing. Maybe a Saturday morning? That's usually a quiet time.",
            "mentions": [
              87396
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A5"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M52",
            "speaker_id": 4543,
            "reply_to": "M48",
            "text": "do we have the tools for woodworking?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M53",
            "speaker_id": 87396,
            "reply_to": "M52",
            "text": "Yes, I've already checked with the home manager. We have a basic kit in the workshop that's been unused for a while. I've checked it and it's safe and suitable for a supervised introductory session. All detailed in A6.",
            "mentions": [
              4543
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
